["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"The Agent Bottleneck Isn&#x27;t Context, It&#x27;s Memory: Write, Change, Recall, Forget Uber burning through its token budget in 13 weeks proves stuffing context is the wrong move; MongoDB points the Agent performance bottleneck at memory — write, change, recall, forget — and suggests starting with employee use cases and humans in the loop. The Cognitive Revolution Cognitive Revolution Write, Change, Recall, Forget: MongoDB&#x27;s Pete Johnson on How Retrieval Drives Agent Performance Agent memory vector retrieval embedding models RAG enterprise AI MongoDB token maxing contextual chunking Matryoshka embedding agent skills\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-01-cogrev-agent-的瓶颈不在上下文-在记忆的写改召回遗忘/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/f2c0e832077f2ab7-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:36:43</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The Cognitive Revolution</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0901</span></div>\n<h2>The Agent Bottleneck Isn&#x27;t Context, It&#x27;s Memory: Write, Change, Recall, Forget</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Uber burning through its token budget in 13 weeks proves stuffing context is the wrong move; MongoDB points the Agent performance bottleneck at memory — write, change, recall, forget — and suggests starting with employee use cases and humans in the loop.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Agent memory</span><span class=\"tag\">vector retrieval</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"The Fed Chair Never Loses a Vote: Warsh Talks Against Guidance, but His Body Is Already Paving the Way for Hikes Posen gives Warsh&#x27;s Jackson Hole speech a B-, arguing that he talks against forward guidance while actually paving the way for hikes, and predicts the Fed will raise rates 75-100 basis points over the next six months. Odd Lots Odd Lots Adam Posen Thinks Things Could Get Very &#x27;Messy&#x27; for the Fed Fed Inflation Central Bank Independence AI Jobs Powell Jackson Hole fiscal dominance fan charts J-curve messy jobs staggered terms\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-01-oddlots-warsh演讲只是b-嘴上反指引-身体要加息/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dbb9160e6d589beb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">59:42</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0901</span></div>\n<h2>The Fed Chair Never Loses a Vote: Warsh Talks Against Guidance, but His Body Is Already Paving the Way for Hikes</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Posen gives Warsh&#x27;s Jackson Hole speech a B-, arguing that he talks against forward guidance while actually paving the way for hikes, and predicts the Fed will raise rates 75-100 basis points over the next six months.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Fed</span><span class=\"tag\">Inflation</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"ECT Is Not Torture: 70% Respond, 60% Remit ECT brings about response in roughly 70% of patients and full symptom remission in 60%; it is not the electric chair of One Flew Over the Cuckoo&#x27;s Nest but the oldest somatic treatment to survive the slaughterhouse, the asylum, and the anti-psychiatry movement. This Podcast Will Kill You This Podcast Will Kill You Ep 220 Electroconvulsive Therapy Part 1: A charged history Psychiatry ECT Depression Medical history Stigma Film and science communication electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) somatic therapy insulin coma therapy Metrosol shock therapy anti-psychiatry movement\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-01-tpwky-ect-不是酷刑-是精神科最有效的疗法之一/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/360c7ded98e41886-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">50:30</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Podcast Will Kill You</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0901</span></div>\n<h2>ECT Is Not Torture: 70% Respond, 60% Remit</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">ECT brings about response in roughly 70% of patients and full symptom remission in 60%; it is not the electric chair of One Flew Over the Cuckoo&#x27;s Nest but the oldest somatic treatment to survive the slaughterhouse, the asylum, and the anti-psychiatry movement.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Psychiatry</span><span class=\"tag\">ECT</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"A State Court Authorized the Security Test, the Sheriff Said the Contract Was Void A state court&#x27;s authorization letter has no power over a county courthouse building, so a contracted security test became burglary. Even after every charge was dropped, the arrest record stays on their files forever — the justice system can pay money, but it cannot restore a clean record. Darknet Diaries Darknet Diaries 179: The Courthouse - Revisited Penetration Testing Physical Security Wrongful Arrest Legal Accountability Immunity Startups qualified immunity sovereign immunity\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-01-darknetdiaries-持州法院授权测安防-警长却说合同无效/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/efb1e077bc2ff15f-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"D\"><span class=\"dur\">1:35:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Darknet Diaries</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0901</span></div>\n<h2>A State Court Authorized the Security Test, the Sheriff Said the Contract Was Void</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A state court&#x27;s authorization letter has no power over a county courthouse building, so a contracted security test became burglary. Even after every charge was dropped, the arrest record stays on their files forever — the justice system can pay money, but it cannot restore a clean record.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Penetration Testing</span><span class=\"tag\">Physical Security</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Residual connections: the most underrated simple hack in deep learning history ResNet is the most cited paper of the 21st century, but its real contribution is not making networks deeper — it invented the residual stream, a kind of working memory that lets a model store and edit information, and that changed how we understand neural networks entirely. WelchLabsVideo WelchLabsVideo The most cited paper of the century is a brilliant hack ResNet Deep learning Transformer Working memory Vision models Architecture Residual stream Skip connection Register tokens Shattered gradients problem\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-01-welchlabsvideo-残差连接-深度学习史上最被低估的简单-hack/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/a540a5f22c57ac52-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"W\"></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">WelchLabsVideo</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0901</span></div>\n<h2>Residual connections: the most underrated simple hack in deep learning history</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">ResNet is the most cited paper of the 21st century, but its real contribution is not making networks deeper — it invented the residual stream, a kind of working memory that lets a model store and edit information, and that changed how we understand neural networks entirely.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">ResNet</span><span class=\"tag\">Deep learning</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"The Fed&#x27;s Credibility Cracks, and the Options Market Shrugs The Fed&#x27;s credibility broke over a single decision not to hike, yet the options market still prices Fed days like any other day — the cheapest insurance may be an illusion. Excess Returns Excess Returns Sticky Inflation. Cheap Volatility. A Less Predictable Fed. Why Aren’t Markets More Worried? Fed Volatility Options Strategy Inflation Midterms AI Writing forward volatility demand-based inflation zero DTE straddle jawboning financial repression calendarized gamma\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-excessreturns-美联储信誉崩塌-期权市场却当无事发生/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/3cac5e72b6049e76-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">1:02:28</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Excess Returns</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>The Fed&#x27;s Credibility Cracks, and the Options Market Shrugs</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The Fed&#x27;s credibility broke over a single decision not to hike, yet the options market still prices Fed days like any other day — the cheapest insurance may be an illusion.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Fed</span><span class=\"tag\">Volatility</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"China&#x27;s Economic Peak Is Behind It: Credit Stalls, Deflation Looms China&#x27;s share of global GDP peaked in 2021 and has fallen since; credit growth has dropped from 18% to 5%, and real growth may be just 1.5%-2%. The US has outperformed for five straight years. The supply-chain-dominance narrative is falsified by the data, and the future looks more like Japanese-style deflation. Geopolitics Decanted with Dmitri Alperovitch Geopolitics Decanted with Dmitri Alperovitch The Miracle Is Over: Inside China&#x27;s Slow-Motion Economic Decay China economy Credit PPP Demographics US-China rivalry Trade protection PPP / Purchasing Power Parity Impossible Trinity Loan Prime Rate (LPR) Special Revenue Bonds Total Factor Productivity (TFP) Demand-side Controls\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-geopoliticsdec-中国经济巅峰已过-美国优势还将扩大/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/8de827bd7254104a-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"G\"><span class=\"dur\">47:58</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\">Geopolitics Decanted with Dmitri Alperovitch</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>China&#x27;s Economic Peak Is Behind It: Credit Stalls, Deflation Looms</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">China&#x27;s share of global GDP peaked in 2021 and has fallen since; credit growth has dropped from 18% to 5%, and real growth may be just 1.5%-2%. The US has outperformed for five straight years. The supply-chain-dominance narrative is falsified by the data, and the future looks more like Japanese-style deflation.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">China economy</span><span class=\"tag\">Credit</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Bell Used Einstein&#x27;s Own Tools to Refute His Central Argument The EPR argument forces you to choose between &quot;the quantum description is incomplete&quot; and &quot;action at a distance&quot;; determinism was never a premise but an inferred conclusion. The full logic of Bell&#x27;s theorem has to start here. Theories of Everything with Curt Jaimungal Theories of Everything with Curt Jaimungal Tim Maudlin: Quantum Nonlocality Explained FROM SCRATCH Quantum Mechanics EPR Bell&#x27;s Theorem Nonlocality History of Physics Action at a Distance EPR / Einstein-Podolsky-Rosen action at a distance configuration space reality criterion ontological locality dynamical locality\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-theoriesofever-贝尔用爱因斯坦自己的工具推翻了他的核心论点/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/06123fc0486c117a-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">3:18:36</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Theories of Everything with Curt Jaimungal</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Bell Used Einstein&#x27;s Own Tools to Refute His Central Argument</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The EPR argument forces you to choose between &quot;the quantum description is incomplete&quot; and &quot;action at a distance&quot;; determinism was never a premise but an inferred conclusion. The full logic of Bell&#x27;s theorem has to start here.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Quantum Mechanics</span><span class=\"tag\">EPR</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"The quantum endgame isn&#x27;t cleaner qubits, it&#x27;s who can mass-produce on a phone-chip line The endgame of quantum computing isn&#x27;t whose qubits are cleaner, it&#x27;s who can mass-produce on existing semiconductor lines; silicon spin qubits reuse TSMC&#x27;s lithography, while trapped ions are stuck at a hundred thousand laser beams and superconductors at warehouse-scale refrigerators. From First Principles From First Principles Why Spin Qubits Will Win the Quantum Race (Part 2) (EP 55) Quantum computing Silicon spin Semiconductors Superconducting Trapped ions AI auto-tuning transmon valley splitting 2DEG DETR exchange-only qubit\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-fromfirstprinc-硅自旋将赢-百万比特只需一块硅晶圆/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/3248f02d6e6be9fe-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"F\"><span class=\"dur\">3:46:20</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">From First Principles</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>The quantum endgame isn&#x27;t cleaner qubits, it&#x27;s who can mass-produce on a phone-chip line</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The endgame of quantum computing isn&#x27;t whose qubits are cleaner, it&#x27;s who can mass-produce on existing semiconductor lines; silicon spin qubits reuse TSMC&#x27;s lithography, while trapped ions are stuck at a hundred thousand laser beams and superconductors at warehouse-scale refrigerators.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Quantum computing</span><span class=\"tag\">Silicon spin</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI chip shipments are about to jump an order of magnitude: from a million units to 15 million Broadcom&#x27;s president lays out the AI chip roadmap: from a million units toward 15 million, with &quot;beast&quot; as the largest package at 8 stackable compute die plus 16 HBM, and four of the five frontier labs working with the company. TechTechPotato TechTechPotato Future GPUs Will Look Like This Custom silicon ASIC Advanced packaging HBM Broadcom Compute supply chain back-end design services HBM CoWoS scaleup fabric\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-techtechpotato-未来-ai-定制芯片的形态-一只带-16-个-hbm-的巨兽/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/7f1cfd222dffd8f1-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">11:10</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">TechTechPotato</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>AI chip shipments are about to jump an order of magnitude: from a million units to 15 million</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Broadcom&#x27;s president lays out the AI chip roadmap: from a million units toward 15 million, with &quot;beast&quot; as the largest package at 8 stackable compute die plus 16 HBM, and four of the five frontier labs working with the company.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Custom silicon</span><span class=\"tag\">ASIC</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"An Explorer Died for a Phantom City, and the Trail Starts with a Political Forgery Percy Fawcett&#x27;s Amazon expeditions are usually told as adventure legend, but the real starting point was a border dispute driven by the rubber trade; his &quot;respect&quot; for Indigenous peoples is badly oversimplified, and the City of Z that consumed him may rest on a forged manuscript. Stuff You Missed in History Class Stuff You Missed in History Class Percy Fawcett, Manuscript 512, and a Lost City in the Amazon, Pt. 1 Exploration history Amazon Rubber trade Indigenous peoples Mysticism Lost city Manuscript 512 Royal Geographical Society rubber boom Mato Grosso City of Z\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-stuffmissed-福西特不是去冒险-是去给橡胶资本画地图/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/88586eb98e196b1a-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">34:06</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Stuff You Missed in History Class</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>An Explorer Died for a Phantom City, and the Trail Starts with a Political Forgery</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Percy Fawcett&#x27;s Amazon expeditions are usually told as adventure legend, but the real starting point was a border dispute driven by the rubber trade; his &quot;respect&quot; for Indigenous peoples is badly oversimplified, and the City of Z that consumed him may rest on a forged manuscript.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Exploration history</span><span class=\"tag\">Amazon</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Time Is Not an Illusion: Irreversibility Is More Fundamental Than Symmetric Equations Jim Al-Khalili argues that time is real and directed, and that irreversibility is more fundamental than time-symmetric equations; he also proposes replacing thermodynamic entropy with quantum entanglement entropy as the basis for the past hypothesis. Sean Carroll&#x27;s Mindscape Mindscape 366 | Jim Al-Khalili on Time, Quantum, Biology, and Cosmology Arrow of Time Quantum Mechanics Quantum Biology Entropy Past Hypothesis Philosophy of Physics past hypothesis entanglement entropy master equation decoherence non-Markovian many-worlds interpretation\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-mindscape-时间的方向性比时间对称方程更根本/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/d69097efcbd03611-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">1:15:16</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Sean Carroll&#x27;s Mindscape</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Time Is Not an Illusion: Irreversibility Is More Fundamental Than Symmetric Equations</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Jim Al-Khalili argues that time is real and directed, and that irreversibility is more fundamental than time-symmetric equations; he also proposes replacing thermodynamic entropy with quantum entanglement entropy as the basis for the past hypothesis.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Arrow of Time</span><span class=\"tag\">Quantum Mechanics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Most Gazans Have Already Abandoned Hamas, and the Disarmament Window Is Opening Gaza-born policy scholar Alkhatib argues from four layers of opposition, two polls and demographic data that most Gazans turned against Hamas long ago and that Hamas may be forced into phased disarmament — but host Russ&#x27;s pessimism is a sharp reminder that disarmament equals political suicide for Hamas. EconTalk EconTalk Hamas and the Future of Gaza (with Ahmed Fouad Alkhatib) Gaza Hamas Israel-Palestine Poll Manipulation Demilitarization Middle East Geopolitics Shikaki polls NCAG Great Reset UNRWA DSA\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-econtalk-加沙多数人已抛弃哈马斯-缴械窗口正在打开/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/f8da698e33560635-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">1:22:48</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">EconTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Most Gazans Have Already Abandoned Hamas, and the Disarmament Window Is Opening</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Gaza-born policy scholar Alkhatib argues from four layers of opposition, two polls and demographic data that most Gazans turned against Hamas long ago and that Hamas may be forced into phased disarmament — but host Russ&#x27;s pessimism is a sharp reminder that disarmament equals political suicide for Hamas.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Gaza</span><span class=\"tag\">Hamas</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"US Economic Resilience Comes From Consumers Borrowing From the Future Barkin breaks down why consumption stays strong despite high prices: consumers cut savings, fall behind on bills and stretch out loan payments to keep spending; AI investment so far is more about price increases and crowding out than a productivity dividend; the Fed may face a long headwind. Odd Lots Odd Lots Richmond Fed’s Tom Barkin on the Surprisingly Resilient Real Economy Consumption resilience Federal Reserve AI capex Inflation Data centers Tariffs SEP / Summary of Economic Projections dot plot R-star / neutral rate forward guidance private label\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-oddlots-美国经济韧性来自消费者向未来借钱/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dbb9160e6d589beb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">31:17</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>US Economic Resilience Comes From Consumers Borrowing From the Future</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Barkin breaks down why consumption stays strong despite high prices: consumers cut savings, fall behind on bills and stretch out loan payments to keep spending; AI investment so far is more about price increases and crowding out than a productivity dividend; the Fed may face a long headwind.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Consumption resilience</span><span class=\"tag\">Federal Reserve</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"The US Treasury Secretary Threatens Allies with Divine Wrath, Proving He Has No Cards Treasury Secretary Bessent paints America as an irritable god and demands allies submit like Pascal&#x27;s wager. Farrell sees through the op-ed: the louder the threat, the more it proves the US has no means of delivery, and allies have already begun to fend for themselves. Hidden Forces Hidden Forces Bessent&#x27;s Wager and Why the World is Calling America&#x27;s Bluff | Henry Farrell Trade War Dollar System Geopolitics US Institutions Financial Sanctions Pascal&#x27;s wager weaponized interdependence flexible realism unitary executive neo-royalism busted flush\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-hiddenforces-美国财长用神罚威胁盟国-反而证明手里没牌/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/2b4203c8f6331570-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"H\"><span class=\"dur\">51:39</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Hidden Forces</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>The US Treasury Secretary Threatens Allies with Divine Wrath, Proving He Has No Cards</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Treasury Secretary Bessent paints America as an irritable god and demands allies submit like Pascal&#x27;s wager. Farrell sees through the op-ed: the louder the threat, the more it proves the US has no means of delivery, and allies have already begun to fend for themselves.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Trade War</span><span class=\"tag\">Dollar System</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Consciousness Has No Finish Line: The Brain Is Multiple Drafts, Not a Screening Room Dennett argues against the &quot;Cartesian Theater&quot;: there is no single finish line where all sensations pour into consciousness; the brain is parallel discriminations, multiple drafts that never get summed up, and even &quot;when did you become conscious of it&quot; often has no factual answer. The Partially Examined Life Partially Examined Life Ep. 399: Dan Dennett&#x27;s Model of Mind (Part One) Consciousness Philosophy Models of Mind Multiple Drafts Cognitive Science Cartesian Theater Multiple Drafts Model Phi phenomenon Qualia Homunculus Stalinesque vs. Orwellian\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-pel-笛卡尔剧场不存在-意识不是放映-而是多重草稿/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/5a66360fe1170966-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">47:34</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Partially Examined Life</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Consciousness Has No Finish Line: The Brain Is Multiple Drafts, Not a Screening Room</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Dennett argues against the &quot;Cartesian Theater&quot;: there is no single finish line where all sensations pour into consciousness; the brain is parallel discriminations, multiple drafts that never get summed up, and even &quot;when did you become conscious of it&quot; often has no factual answer.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Consciousness</span><span class=\"tag\">Philosophy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"The hard part of dementia care isn&#x27;t the patient — it&#x27;s the caregiver being ground down The hard part of dementia care isn&#x27;t the illness itself but the caregiver worn down day after day — care turns a wife into a nurse and makes a millennial quit her job; love is the starting point but not the support, and the system hasn&#x27;t caught these families yet. 不合时宜 不合时宜 漫长的告别：失智症、照护者与终将老去的我们 Dementia Elder care Caregivers Long-term care insurance Aging Only children Hogeweyk The Soul of Care informal care long-term care insurance wet-on-wet watercolor\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-cn300980-失智照护的难不在失智老人-而在会被拖垮的照护者/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/bda8c0f9bba83da6-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"不\"><span class=\"dur\">1:04:00</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">不合时宜</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>The hard part of dementia care isn&#x27;t the patient — it&#x27;s the caregiver being ground down</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The hard part of dementia care isn&#x27;t the illness itself but the caregiver worn down day after day — care turns a wife into a nurse and makes a millennial quit her job; love is the starting point but not the support, and the system hasn&#x27;t caught these families yet.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Dementia</span><span class=\"tag\">Elder care</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"The fab bottleneck isn&#x27;t the lithography tool — it&#x27;s the OHT cars on the ceiling What really caps wafer fab capacity isn&#x27;t just lithography tools, but the OHT cars running back and forth on the ceiling. The 300mm transition made them mandatory, and today the market is a Daifuku–Muratec duopoly. Asianometry Asianometry The Little Ceiling Robots Inside a Semiconductor Fab AMHS OHT Semiconductor Manufacturing Wafer Fabs Automated Logistics Equipment Monopoly AMHS / Automated Material Handling System FOUP / Front Opening Unified Pod OHT / Overhead Hoist Transport Stocker Interbay / Intrabay\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-asianometry-别只盯着光刻机-天花板上的-oht-小车也在卡产能/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/c6301489e9b3f727-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">20:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Asianometry</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>The fab bottleneck isn&#x27;t the lithography tool — it&#x27;s the OHT cars on the ceiling</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">What really caps wafer fab capacity isn&#x27;t just lithography tools, but the OHT cars running back and forth on the ceiling. The 300mm transition made them mandatory, and today the market is a Daifuku–Muratec duopoly.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AMHS</span><span class=\"tag\">OHT</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"The Treasury Secretary Trades the Bond Market Like a Position, and Prices Win in the End US Treasury Secretary Bessent is intervening in the bond market, trade and sanctions with a trader&#x27;s mindset, but inflation and deficits keep pushing prices up, and his strategy may come to nothing. Patrick Boyle Patrick Boyle Scott Bessent Is at War With Prices — and Prices Are Winning! Treasury bonds Fiscal policy Inflation Federal Reserve Crypto Trade war TGA (Treasury General Account) On-the-run vs off-the-run bonds Duration neutral Term premium Stablecoin\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-patrickboyle-贝森特与价格的战争-财政部长的宏观赌局/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/2eb71149af422d0e-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">44:51</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Patrick Boyle</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>The Treasury Secretary Trades the Bond Market Like a Position, and Prices Win in the End</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">US Treasury Secretary Bessent is intervening in the bond market, trade and sanctions with a trader&#x27;s mindset, but inflation and deficits keep pushing prices up, and his strategy may come to nothing.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Treasury bonds</span><span class=\"tag\">Fiscal policy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Elite Universities Are a Cartel: They Sell Status, Not Education America&#x27;s elite universities are not charitable educational institutions but a cartel that maintains its brand by freezing enrollment, running alumni donations, and absorbing federal research grants; they sell status, not education. Modern MBA Modern MBA The American College Cartel University Finance Endowments Elite Education Admissions US Innovation endowment advancement provost tenure yield tech tree\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-modernmba-精英大学是制造稀缺的卡特尔-而非教育机构/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/3676f3a101faa05c-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"M\"><span class=\"dur\">45:11</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Modern MBA</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Elite Universities Are a Cartel: They Sell Status, Not Education</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">America&#x27;s elite universities are not charitable educational institutions but a cartel that maintains its brand by freezing enrollment, running alumni donations, and absorbing federal research grants; they sell status, not education.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">University Finance</span><span class=\"tag\">Endowments</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Phage Hedges Its Bets With 10,000-Fold Reversion, and the First Humanized EBV Antibody Phages hedge their bets through 10,000-fold reversion in SSRs, humanized EBV antibodies block tumors in vivo, and vaccine efforts advance on multiple fronts. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1353: Phage bet-hedging and EBV antibodies Phage Bet-hedging EBV Antibodies Vaccines Cognitive laziness SSR / simple sequence repeat bet-hedging contingency locus hybridoma\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-twiv-噬菌体用随机突变下注-ebv人类抗体首次成功/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><div class=\"fallback\">T</div><span class=\"dur\">1:52:21</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Phage Hedges Its Bets With 10,000-Fold Reversion, and the First Humanized EBV Antibody</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Phages hedge their bets through 10,000-fold reversion in SSRs, humanized EBV antibodies block tumors in vivo, and vaccine efforts advance on multiple fronts.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Phage</span><span class=\"tag\">Bet-hedging</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Phages Hedge Their Bets by Slipping During Replication, Wagering That Bacterial Defenses Will Escalate Slippage is not a replication defect but a phage hedge: a minority of individuals in the population shift reading frame through repeat-sequence changes, generating variants that have not yet been selected. Most fit the current environment; when bacterial defenses escalate, the low-frequency alternatives take over. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1353: Phage bet-hedging and EBV antibodies Phage Bet-hedging EBV Monoclonal antibodies Vaccine design Science communication simple sequence repeats (SSR) bet-hedging hybridoma HAT medium humanized mice\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-twiv-噬菌体靠复制打滑预留变异-赌细菌防御会升级/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.microbe.tv/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/TWiV_v3_white.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:52:01</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Phages Hedge Their Bets by Slipping During Replication, Wagering That Bacterial Defenses Will Escalate</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Slippage is not a replication defect but a phage hedge: a minority of individuals in the population shift reading frame through repeat-sequence changes, generating variants that have not yet been selected. Most fit the current environment; when bacterial defenses escalate, the low-frequency alternatives take over.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Phage</span><span class=\"tag\">Bet-hedging</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"When Code Is Free, You Pay for Judgment and Distribution Replit&#x27;s head of engineering offers a test: once code is free, only trust, data, infrastructure, atoms and networks survive. Non-programmers are using domain knowledge to build $180K-a-month businesses in three days. Peter Yang Peter Yang How Non-Coders Are Vibe Coding $100K+ Businesses with AI | Amol Jain vibe coding AI startups SaaS Replit model neutrality enterprise-built software Vibe coding TAM System of record MCP Token maxing\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-peteryang-代码成本归零后-用户为判断力与分发付费/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/e9c1f372be129004-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">36:35</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Peter Yang</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>When Code Is Free, You Pay for Judgment and Distribution</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Replit&#x27;s head of engineering offers a test: once code is free, only trust, data, infrastructure, atoms and networks survive. Non-programmers are using domain knowledge to build $180K-a-month businesses in three days.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">vibe coding</span><span class=\"tag\">AI startups</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI&#x27;s third era is the persistent co-worker, and product cycles last only three months OpenAI product lead Tara Seshan argues that AI products are moving from chat to agents to persistent co-workers, and that builders must design for model capabilities two to three months out; the future of work is steering, not rowing, and the writing that is thinking should never be automated. Lenny&#x27;s Podcast Lenny&#x27;s Podcast AI’s third era: the rise of persistent AI coworkers | Tara Seshan (OpenAI’s product lead) Product cycles Persistent co-worker Codex Writing as thinking Product marketing fit persistent co-worker product marketing fit\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-lennys-ai-第三纪元是持久协作者-产品周期只有三个月/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/67bb7dafb90c60da-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"L\"><span class=\"dur\">1:21:44</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Lenny&#x27;s Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>AI&#x27;s third era is the persistent co-worker, and product cycles last only three months</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">OpenAI product lead Tara Seshan argues that AI products are moving from chat to agents to persistent co-workers, and that builders must design for model capabilities two to three months out; the future of work is steering, not rowing, and the writing that is thinking should never be automated.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Product cycles</span><span class=\"tag\">Persistent co-worker</span>\n</div></div></a>"]